+# Contract: Codex Hook Manifests (host-facing registration)
+
+**Feature**: [../spec.md](../spec.md) | **Surface**: JSON hook-registration manifests read by the
+Codex host at plugin load/install time.
+
+**Files** (byte-identical pair — a core invariant of this contract):
+
+- `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/codex-hooks.json`
+- `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/codex-hooks.json`
+
+The companion copy is the one the `graphhelm-codex-hooks` package exposes to Codex via
+`.codex-plugin/plugin.json` (`"hooks": "./hooks/codex-hooks.json"`). The main-plugin copy exists so
+Codex-capable installations of `graphhelm` carry the same declaration; both must always be
+identical byte for byte, verified by `test_codex_compatibility_package_keeps_one_hook_source`
+(raw-byte comparison) and by hash checks (quickstart.md C3).
+
+## Normative content after this feature
+
+```json
+{
+  "hooks": {
+    "SessionStart": [
+      {
+        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
+        "hooks": [
+          {
+            "type": "command",
+            "command": "python \"${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py\" start --host codex",
+            "statusMessage": "Loading Keel and GraphHelm context",
+            "timeout": 5,
+            "additionalContextLimit": 512
+          }
+        ]
+      }
+    ],
+    "SessionEnd": [
+      {
+        "hooks": [
+          {
+            "type": "command",
+            "command": "python \"${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py\" end --host codex",
+            "timeout": 3
+          }
+        ]
+      }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The only difference from the currently shipped file is `"timeout": 3` in the SessionEnd entry
+(was `5`).
+
+## Invariants (must hold after the change)
+
+1. **Declared Codex SessionEnd timeout equals the host cap**: `3` seconds, matching the Codex
+   hard cap (FR-001, SC-001). A declared value above the cap advertises a window the host never
+   grants — that mismatch is the defect this feature removes.
+2. **Every other entry unchanged**: SessionStart matcher, command, statusMessage, timeout (5),
+   additionalContextLimit (512); SessionEnd command and type (US2-AS1).
+3. **Twin byte identity**: the two copies compare equal as raw bytes (FR-006).
+4. **Companion pins unchanged**: no `plugin.json` at the companion root; `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`
+   keeps its hooks pointer and its version equal to the main plugin's (all four plugin manifests'
+   versions stay equal).
+5. **Claude manifest untouched**: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/hooks.json` keeps five-second timeouts
+   on both events (FR-002); baseline SHA-256 `5FA2B622D3B35AE4BD40E07B49F0C319BA630699A6C2813CE5E1A684E758FB4D`.
+6. **Documented equality**: the README budget paragraph states exactly these figures
+   (SC-005); declared, effective, and documented budgets agree for every event/host pair.
