+# Data Model: Fix Codex SessionEnd Hook Budget
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-27
+
+Entities below are the data-bearing artifacts this feature touches or freezes. For each: fields,
+what changes, validation rules, and (where applicable) state transitions. Contracts for the
+host-facing and script-facing surfaces live in [contracts/](contracts/).
+
+## Entity 1 — Codex hook manifest (two byte-identical copies)
+
+- **Paths**: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/codex-hooks.json`, `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/codex-hooks.json`
+- **Relationships**: raw-byte-identical pair enforced by `test_codex_compatibility_package_keeps_one_hook_source`; referenced by `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/.codex-plugin/plugin.json` (`"hooks": "./hooks/codex-hooks.json"`).
+- **Changes in this feature**: one field only — `hooks.SessionEnd[0].hooks[0].timeout`: `5 → 3`.
+
+| Field (JSON pointer) | Type | Before | After | Rule |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `/hooks/SessionStart/0/matcher` | string | `"startup\|resume\|clear\|compact"` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionStart/0/hooks/0/type` | string | `"command"` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionStart/0/hooks/0/command` | string | `python "${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py" start --host codex` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionStart/0/hooks/0/statusMessage` | string | `"Loading Keel and GraphHelm context"` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionStart/0/hooks/0/timeout` | number | `5` | unchanged | invariant (SessionStart out of scope) |
+| `/hooks/SessionStart/0/hooks/0/additionalContextLimit` | number | `512` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionEnd/0/hooks/0/type` | string | `"command"` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionEnd/0/hooks/0/command` | string | `python "${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py" end --host codex` | unchanged | invariant |
+| `/hooks/SessionEnd/0/hooks/0/timeout` | number | `5` | **`3`** | FR-001: equals the Codex host cap |
+
+**Validation**: valid JSON object of the same shape; integer seconds; both copies byte-identical
+after the edit (SC-001). All other keys and their order/formatting preserved.
+
+## Entity 2 — Claude hook manifest (invariant)
+
+- **Path**: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/hooks.json`
+- **Changes**: none. `SessionStart` timeout stays `5`, `SessionEnd` timeout stays `5` (FR-002);
+  the `--host claude` commands and `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` references are untouched.
+- **Baseline**: SHA-256 `5FA2B622D3B35AE4BD40E07B49F0C319BA630699A6C2813CE5E1A684E758FB4D`
+  (measured 2026-10-27); a post-change hash comparison against this value is check C4 in quickstart.md.
+
+## Entity 3 — Session hook script (two byte-identical copies)
+
+- **Paths**: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py`, `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/session_hook.py`
+- **Relationships**: raw-byte-identical pair, same enforcing test; the companion copy is the one
+  Codex actually runs.
+- **Changes in this feature**:
+
+| Item | Kind | Before | After | Constraint source |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| module constant block (near `MAX_*` bounds) | new constant | — | `END_ACK_TIMEOUT = 2.0` with budget comment | FR-003/FR-004, SC-002; decision D1/D2 |
+| `_end_impl` end-request call site (`session_hook.py:351`) | call argument | inline literal `timeout=3.0` | `timeout=END_ACK_TIMEOUT` | FR-003 |
+| `request(...)` signature default | parameter default | `timeout: float = 1.0` | unchanged | SessionStart briefing bound is frozen (spec Assumptions) |
+
+- **Validation rules (unchanged behavior this feature must preserve)**: input ≤ 64 KiB; reply ≤ 256 KiB;
+  state ≤ 32 KiB; context ≤ 1600 chars; token file ≤ 4096 bytes; plain-HTTP Runtime must be loopback;
+  redirects refused; state files mode 0600 / dirs 0700 on POSIX.
+- **Twin identity**: after editing, both copies byte-identical (FR-006); baseline pre-edit SHA-256
+  `67A7B1CE…E95` recorded in [research.md](research.md) for reference only.
+
+## Entity 4 — Delivery receipt (local hook state, invariant schema)
+
+- **Storage**: `<state-root>/<sha256(v2\0execution\0session\0host\0origin)>.json`, version 2; sibling `.lock` file.
+- **Format**: frozen by this feature (no migration — spec Assumptions).
+
+| Field | Type | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `version` | int | must be `2` |
+| `executionId` / `sessionId` / `host` / `origin` | strings | must equal current binding identity or the receipt is rejected as mismatched |
+| `briefing` | object (optional) | revalidated through `_briefing_digest` on read; unknown fields dropped |
+| `delivery` | object (optional) | see below |
+| `delivery.signalId` | string | `session-end-v2-` + first 24 hex chars of the identity digest — identical across retries (idempotency key) |
+| `delivery.signal` | object | canonical `agent_session_ended` signal; stored bytes replayed identically on every retry; revalidated on read |
+| `delivery.declaredNodeId` | string\|null | optional, ID-shaped |
+| `delivery.delivered` | bool | delivery state flag |
+
+**State transitions** (unchanged by this feature — documented so the plan's "what must keep
+working" is explicit):
+
+```text
+(receipt absent)
+   │  first end event, undelivered
+   ▼
+delivery.delivered = false ──matching ack (executionId+signalId, ok:true)──▶ delivery.delivered = true
+   │                                                                            (terminal; later ends skip sending)
+   │  timeout at END_ACK_TIMEOUT, refusal (ok != true), mismatched ack,
+   │  corrupt receipt, busy lock, binding mismatch
+   ▼
+unchanged receipt; operation reported "unobserved"; next end event retries
+the identical signal body with the identical Idempotency-Key
+```
+
+- **Locking**: non-blocking OS lock on the sibling `.lock` inode; released by the OS when the host
+  kills the process; the inode is intentionally kept (unlinking could let two processes lock two
+  files). Overlapping callers report unobserved; exactly one durable delivery results (covered by
+  `test_overlapping_end_calls_keep_one_signal_body`, `test_killed_end_hook_releases_lock_and_retries_same_signal`).
+- **Failure discipline**: a partially-delivered state is never observable — either the matching ack
+  landed and `delivered` is durably true, or nothing changed and the signal remains retryable.
+
+## Entity 5 — Budget paragraph (plugin README prose)
+
+- **Path**: `plugins/graphhelm/README.md`, Session-hooks section, lines 57–61 (numbered for the
+  current file).
+- **Content contract after the change**: states (a) Codex caps the SessionEnd command process at
+  three seconds and the Codex manifests declare exactly that; (b) Claude keeps its five-second
+  bound; (c) the end-acknowledgement wait is sized to complete inside the Codex cap; and no longer
+  states that both hosts bound the SessionEnd command process to five seconds. Every figure in the
+  paragraph equals the shipped manifests/constant (SC-005). English-only per AGENTS.md.
+- **Frozen neighbours**: the one-second SessionStart socket limit sentence and the
+  unobserved-timeout sentences stay verbatim.
