+# Quickstart / Validation Guide: Fix Codex SessionEnd Hook Budget
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Plan**: [plan.md](plan.md)
+
+Runnable validation scenarios proving the feature end-to-end from this checkout. Prerequisites:
+Python 3.11+ on `PATH` (verified here: 3.11.9), the repository checked out, Windows PowerShell or
+bash. No network access, Docker, credentials, provider accounts, or browser sessions are needed —
+the suite runs an in-process loopback Runtime.
+
+Run every scenario from the repository root. **Report each item as passed, failed, or unobserved
+— never skip-as-pass.** Details on what each scenario proves (and the one thing only a real Codex
+host could prove) are in [research.md](research.md), section D6.
+
+## S1 — Hook contract suite (primary observer; FR-008, SC-003/SC-004)
+
+```powershell
+python -m unittest plugins.graphhelm.hooks.test_session_hook
+```
+
+**Expected**: `Ran 28 tests … OK`, exit code 0, zero failures and zero skips. This single module
+drives the real script through subprocesses against an in-process Runtime and covers, among others:
+an acknowledgement released ~1.25 s after the POST must be confirmed from one request
+(`test_end_accepts_slow_matching_ack_without_extra_posts` — the FR-004 observer under the new
+bound), refusal/mismatch staying retryable with identical signal bytes and idempotency key,
+overlapping ends, the killed-hook lock release, corrupt-receipt fail-closed behavior, and raw-byte
+twin identity of both `session_hook.py` copies and both `codex-hooks.json` files
+(`test_codex_compatibility_package_keeps_one_hook_source` — part of SC-001's observer).
+
+## C2 — Declared budgets match the effective host budgets (FR-001/FR-002, SC-001)
+
+```powershell
+$m  = Get-Content plugins\graphhelm\hooks\codex-hooks.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
+$c  = Get-Content plugins\graphhelm-codex-hooks\hooks\codex-hooks.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
+$k  = Get-Content plugins\graphhelm\hooks\hooks.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
+@($m.hooks.SessionEnd[0].hooks[0].timeout,   $c.hooks.SessionEnd[0].hooks[0].timeout)  | Should-Budget 3   # Codex SessionEnd = 3
+@($m.hooks.SessionStart[0].hooks[0].timeout, $k.hooks.SessionStart[0].hooks[0].timeout,
+   $k.hooks.SessionEnd[0].hooks[0].timeout) | Should-Budget 5                                           # everything else = 5
+```
+
+(`Should-Budget` is shorthand: assert every listed value equals the right-hand number.)
+**Expected**: both Codex manifests declare SessionEnd `3`; SessionStart stays `5` everywhere; the
+Claude manifest keeps `5` on both events.
+
+## C3 — Twin-file byte identity (FR-006, SC-001)
+
+```powershell
+Get-FileHash plugins\graphhelm\hooks\session_hook.py, plugins\graphhelm-codex-hooks\hooks\session_hook.py | Select-Object Hash
+Get-FileHash plugins\graphhelm\hooks\codex-hooks.json, plugins\graphhelm-codex-hooks\hooks\codex-hooks.json | Select-Object Hash
+```
+
+**Expected**: the two hashes in each pair are equal. (Redundant with S1's compatibility test on
+purpose: it stands alone if the suite is unavailable.)
+
+## C4 — Claude manifest untouched (FR-002)
+
+```powershell
+git diff --stat -- plugins/graphhelm/hooks/hooks.json
+```
+
+**Expected**: empty output. Cross-check:
+`(Get-FileHash plugins\graphhelm\hooks\hooks.json -Algorithm SHA256).Hash` equals the recorded
+baseline `5FA2B622D3B35AE4BD40E07B49F0C319BA630699A6C2813CE5E1A684E758FB4D`.
+
+## C5 — End-acknowledgement bound strictly inside the Codex cap (FR-003/FR-004, SC-002)
+
+```powershell
+Select-String -Path plugins\graphhelm\hooks\session_hook.py, plugins\graphhelm-codex-hooks\hooks\session_hook.py -Pattern 'END_ACK_TIMEOUT|timeout=3\.0|timeout: float = 1\.0'
+```
+
+**Expected**, per file: one definition line `END_ACK_TIMEOUT = 2.0`, exactly one use
+(`timeout=END_ACK_TIMEOUT` in `_end_impl`), and `request(...)` still defaulting to
+`timeout: float = 1.0`; **zero** matches for the old inline literal `timeout=3.0`. The defined
+value must satisfy `1.0 < END_ACK_TIMEOUT < 3.0` — which `2.0` does; the margin arithmetic and the
+rejected alternatives are in [research.md](research.md), D1.
+
+## C6 — Documented budgets equal shipped budgets (FR-007, SC-005)
+
+Read the Session-hooks budget paragraph in `plugins/graphhelm/README.md` (around lines 57–62) and
+compare every figure against C2 (Codex SessionEnd 3, Claude 5) and C5 (two-second end-ack wait).
+Programmatic guard for the removed false sentence:
+
+```powershell
+Select-String -Path plugins\graphhelm\README.md -Pattern 'Both hosts bound'
+```
+
+**Expected**: no match. **Passed** means: the paragraph states the three-second Codex SessionEnd
+cap (now declared in the Codex manifests), the unchanged five-second Claude bound, and that the
+end-acknowledgement wait fits inside the Codex cap — and nothing in it contradicts C2/C5.
+
+## S4 — Optional: wall-time probe for the near-bound end run (evidence for the sizing assumption)
+
+The hard three-second kill is enforced by the Codex host and cannot be reproduced in this
+checkout (unobserved locally; research.md D6). What *can* be measured here is that the worst
+in-window run — an acknowledgement arriving just inside the 2.0 s bound — finishes well under
+three seconds of wall time, startup and durable write included. Save the snippet below as
+`end-timing-probe.py` (scratch location, e.g. under `$env:TEMP`) and run `python end-timing-probe.py`
+from the repository root; remove it afterward.
+
+```python
+import json, os, subprocess, sys, tempfile, threading, time
+from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer
+from pathlib import Path
+
+SCRIPT, DELAY, CAP = Path("plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py"), 1.9, 3.0
+
+class H(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
+    posts = 0
+    def do_POST(self):
+        body = json.loads(self.rfile.read(int(self.headers["Content-Length"])))
+        H.posts += 1
+        time.sleep(DELAY)                      # ack arrives just inside the 2.0 s inactivity bound
+        self.send_response(200)
+        self.send_header("Content-Type", "application/json")
+        self.end_headers()
+        self.wfile.write(json.dumps({"ok": True, "data": {"executionId": "run-probe",
+                                                          "signalId": body["signal"]["id"]}}).encode())
+    def log_message(self, *_): pass
+
+srv = ThreadingHTTPServer(("127.0.0.1", 0), H)
+threading.Thread(target=srv.serve_forever, daemon=True).start()
+tmp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp())
+(tmp / "events.token").write_text("probe-token")
+env = {**os.environ, "GRAPHHELM_EXECUTION_ID": "run-probe",
+       "GRAPHHELM_TOKEN_FILE": str(tmp / "events.token"),
+       "GRAPHHELM_HOOK_STATE_DIR": str(tmp / "state"),
+       "GRAPHHELM_RUNTIME_URL": f"http://127.0.0.1:{srv.server_port}"}
+env.pop("GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID", None); env.pop("GRAPHHELM_NODE_ID", None)
+
+t0 = time.monotonic()
+p = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(SCRIPT), "end", "--host", "codex"],
+                   input=json.dumps({"hook_event_name": "SessionEnd", "session_id": "probe-1"}),
+                   text=True, capture_output=True, env=env, timeout=8)
+wall = time.monotonic() - t0
+delivered = json.loads(next(Path(env["GRAPHHELM_HOOK_STATE_DIR"]).glob("*.json")).read_text())["delivery"]["delivered"]
+print(f"wall={wall:.2f}s rc={p.returncode} delivered={delivered} posts={H.posts} stderr={p.stderr.strip()!r}")
+assert p.returncode == 0 and delivered is True and H.posts == 1 and wall < CAP
+print(f"PASS: near-bound ack confirmed from one request in {wall:.2f}s (< {CAP:.0f}s)")
+```
+
+**Expected**: exit 0 of the probe, e.g. `wall≈2.1–2.3s … delivered=True posts=1`, i.e. wall time
+strictly under the 3.0 s cap with ≥ 0.5 s of headroom on this machine. For the missed-window
+variant, raise `DELAY` to 3.0: the hook then exits 0 in ~2.2 s with `unobserved` on stderr and
+`delivered=False`, and a repeated end run POSTs the same signal bytes with the same
+`Idempotency-Key` (full semantics already covered by S1's retry tests). A machine where the probe
+exceeds 3.0 s invalidates the sizing assumption and must be reported as such — not worked around
+by silently lowering `END_ACK_TIMEOUT` without re-checking C5/S1.
+
