+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: Depends on all desired user stories being complete (T012 depends on T006, T009, T011)
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **User Story 1 (P1)**: Can start after Foundational (Phase 2) — no dependencies on other stories (owns the two `session_hook.py` copies)
+- **User Story 2 (P2)**: Can start after Foundational (Phase 2) — no dependencies on other stories (owns the two `codex-hooks.json` copies); its suite checkpoint (T009) also observes US1's changes but needs nothing from US1 to pass
+- **User Story 3 (P3)**: Can start after Foundational (Phase 2) — owns `plugins/graphhelm/README.md`; its figures must describe the post-US1/US2 state (three-second Codex cap, two-second end-ack wait), so *verify* US3 after US1 and US2 land, though the edit itself may be drafted independently
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Models/entities: none — this feature modifies existing JSON manifests, an existing script, and an existing README paragraph; no new surface beyond the single `END_ACK_TIMEOUT` constant
+- Implementation before verification; verification (suite + inspection checks) completes the story
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- T001 and T002 in Phase 1 (different concerns: suite run vs. hash recording)
+- T004 and T005 in Phase 3 (twin script copies — identical edit, different files; re-check hash equality in T006)
+- T007 and T008 in Phase 4 (twin manifest copies — identical edit, different files; re-check hash equality in T009)
+- Entire user-story phases run concurrently with different workers, since no two stories touch the same file
